rk! Email a link to this job to a friend that is looking for a new opportunity. First Name (required) 7f081762 Last Name (required) 5f16f261 Email (required) 0a1f27ee Referral ea90b33b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Not The Job You Were Looking For? See a list of other jobs you might like below. Assistant Athletic Trainer On Campus Director of Athletics About Us: Colorado College (“CC”) is a private, four-year, highly selective liberal arts college of 2,100 undergraduate students and a small Master of Arts in teaching program. It is located on a 99-acre campus adjacent to downtown, ‘Olympic City’, Colorado Springs. The campus sits on the Front Range of the Rocky Mountains at the foot of Pikes Peak. The college operates an innovative curricular approach, known as the Block Plan, which entails students taking one course at a time for three and a half weeks, with the academic year divided into eight “blocks.” The Colorado College Department of Athletics sponsors 17 varsity programs. Fifteen programs compete at the NCAA Division III level and two at the Division I level. Division III programs are members of the Southern Collegiate Athletic Conference (SCAC), with the exception of Men’s Lacrosse (independent) and Women’s Lacrosse (WIAC affiliate). Division I Men’s Hockey is a member of the National Collegiate Hockey Conference (NCHC) and Division I Women’s Soccer competes as an affiliate member of the Mountain West Conference (MWC).  \n\nThe purpose of this role is to provide education, independent health care, and preventative services for our varsity student-athletes, coaching staff, and members of the Athletic Department.  Work closely with other full-time athletic trainers, physical therapist, and the athletic insurance coordinator to assist in the day-to-day management of the athletic department’s intercollegiate sports medicine operation and provide effective delivery of athletic training services. Assistant Professor of Film and Media Studies On Campus Humanities Division Assistant Professor of Film and Media Studies Accounts Payable Specialist On Campus Finance The Accounts Payable Specialist supports the College's financial operations through the accurate, timely, and compliant processing of accounts payable transactions. This role serves as a key resource for purchasing, P-Card administration, vendor management, payment processes, and customer service while supporting strong internal controls and effective financial stewardship. Responsibilities within these functional areas may be assigned, redistributed, or shared among team members based on business needs, workload, staffing levels, and individual expertise. Executive Writer & Editor On Campus Communications & Marketing The Executive Writer & Editor plays a central role in shaping Colorado College’s voice through high-quality, high-impact content that supports institutional priorities and elevates executive and College visibility. Reporting to the Director of Institutional Communications, this position is responsible for writing, editing, and editorial strategy support across executive communications, internal messaging, public relations, marketing, and campus-wide content needs. This includes serving as the principle writer for presidential and executive remarks as well as supporting communications on major initiatives and providing editorial services and style oversight in alignment with college brand messaging. \n\nThe role is both strategic and executional, requiring exceptional writing, editorial judgment, and collaboration to ensure communications are clear, compelling, and aligned with the college’s voice and values. Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of